cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use ctis in your research, please cite it using these metadata."
type: software
title: ctis
abstract: >-
  ctis is a Python library for simulating and inverting observations from
  computed tomography imaging spectrographs (CTISs), particularly instruments
  that observe the Sun in the extreme ultraviolet. A CTIS records several
  dispersed projections of a spectral scene at once, and ctis reconstructs the
  scene from those images. Instrument models range from an idealized
  instrument characterized by its effective area and dispersion to forward
  models built from optika optical systems, and scenes are reconstructed
  using the multiplicative algebraic reconstruction technique (MART). The
  library also provides synthetic test scenes and merit functions for
  evaluating the quality of an inversion, and it is built on named-arrays, so
  scenes, instruments, and images carry named axes and physical units.
